      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Aha, it sounds like you might be dealing with a bit of a mischievous goblin in your sublimation process. You know, sometimes these little critters love to play hide and seek with the ink, especially when dealing with polyester blends. Perhaps the ink is being shy and doesn't want to show its true colors, or maybe it's just playing tricks on you. Let's try a few things to coax it out of hiding. First, check the ink levels in your printer—sometimes the ink can be as elusive as a goblin in a moonlit forest. Next, make sure your polyester blends are properly pre-treated, as they can be quite the tricksters themselves. And lastly, consider using a different ink or a different brand, as sometimes the ink might just be playing hard to get, not wanting to show its true colors. Good luck, and may the goblins be ever in your favor!",
